From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-client: a WoW64 program's shared-memory buffer is placed again

Patch 0014 refused a placed mapping (VK_EXT_map_memory_placed) of the owner's shared memory: over the bare
reservation PS5_Proton's win32u hands over, that memory reads as the reservation, and Wine's direct-memory engine
took the range for its own. A 32-bit program's buffers fall back to shared memory once the owner refuses direct
memory, and then every map failed: DXVK's D3D11 device was not made ("Failed to map Vulkan memory:
VK_ERROR_MEMORY_MAP_FAILED", host-dmem-fallback64, v2-backend-gate-2026-10-15). PS5_Proton's Wine now keeps the range
it lends for a placed mapping as foreign by record (Wine patch 1130, __wine_ps5_dmem_lend), whatever the kernel shows
there, so the client keeps the descriptor of a shared-memory buffer again (only when the application asked,
ps5_gpu_client_keep_sources, closed when the buffer is freed) and places it as it places direct memory. 0014's free
order is kept.

Host: tests/test_crash_replays.c ("placed shared memory": placed, a protection change there refused and the mapping
kept, the release after the unmap kept reserved). Console: not yet run.

Base: PS5_Vulkan f410e67a + 0001-0015.
